From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:37:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1694/3799] soh: rename func_80044340 -> Camera_BGCheckPos

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the thin wrapper: runs the same background check between two points and writes the corrected position back into the second.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_camera.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_camera.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_camera.c b/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
index 28d917f9e..ed0e2736f 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
@@ -346,7 +346,8 @@ s32 func_80043F94(Camera* camera, Vec3f* from, CamColChk* to) {
     return 1;
 }
 
-void func_80044340(Camera* camera, Vec3f* arg1, Vec3f* arg2) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80044340: the thin wrapper: runs the same background check between two points and writes the corrected position back into the second.
+void Camera_BGCheckPos(Camera* camera, Vec3f* arg1, Vec3f* arg2) {
     CamColChk sp20;
     Vec3s unused;
 
@@ -4419,7 +4420,7 @@ s32 Camera_Subj3(Camera* camera) {
         if (!camera->play->envCtx.skyboxDisabled) {
             Camera_BGCheck(camera, at, eye);
         } else {
-            func_80044340(camera, at, eye);
+            Camera_BGCheckPos(camera, at, eye);  // was func_80044340 [LLM:HIGH]
         }
     } else {
         sp58 = Math_SinS(-sp60.rot.x);
